# The scaffold's own ignore rules are shipped content now: they travel as
# `scaffold/gitignore` and are emitted as .gitignore, because npm pack drops
# every file with that name from a tarball. So they no longer govern this
# tree, and the transient output of working inside the template is listed
# here — one directory up, where the scaffold never copies it (found live:
# npm pack --dry-run listed scaffold/system/site/out/, 2026-08-18).
# `.ksor/` holds ksor's scratch AND two governance files that are the record
# (record spec §1); the directory form cannot be negated, so the glob is
# `.ksor/*` with the two un-ignored — the same shape the emitted .gitignore
# carries. npm-packlist honours this file, so an ignored `.ksor/` would also
# drop the policy from the tarball (found live 2026-08-25).
scaffold/.ksor/*
!scaffold/.ksor/governance.yaml
!scaffold/.ksor/people.yaml
!scaffold/.ksor/takedowns.yaml
scaffold/**/node_modules/
scaffold/system/site/.next/
scaffold/system/site/.source/
scaffold/system/site/out/
scaffold/**/*.tsbuildinfo
scaffold/.env*
scaffold/**/.DS_Store
scaffold/system/site/.staged-knowledge/
scaffold/system/site/.staged-knowledge.lock
